{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1487877-minnesota-a-land-of-wolves-lakes-and-song","id":1487877,"title":"Minnesota, a land of wolves, lakes and song.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-25T06:33:21-07:00","id":1487877,"title":"Minnesota, a land of wolves, lakes and song.","content":"<a href=\"https://www.startribune.com/minnesota-wolves-predators-research-survival-extinction-preservation/600184286/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.startribune.com/minnesot...ion/600184286/</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Something that always puzzled me about the various editions of Werewolf was the dearth of information on the wolves of Minnesota. There are over two thousand wolves here. Two thousand, likely more and their numbers are growing. Their territories are spreading. <br /> <br /> There are stories here.<br /> <br /> Of boundaries between wilderness, cities and farms. Forests deep and ancient. Lakes that reflect the stars. Each an invitation to hear their stories and the howls that ring like song.<br /> <br /> But Minnesota is more than a land of cold, Vikings and lakes. It\u2019s a story of its first peoples, and also it\u2019s immigrants, including Hmong and Somalis who add their perspectives to the land they now call home.<br /> <br /> There are so many stories here, waiting to be told.<br /> <br /> Perhaps one day, one of you will share them, and in time we shall be forsaken no more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26663,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26663-wandering-dreamer","user":"Wandering Dreamer","date":". 07-25-2022, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26663-wandering-dreamer","name":"Wandering Dreamer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","